{"title": "Acanthopale", "html": "\n<div class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">For the genus of worms with this name, see <a data-title=\"Acanthopale (annelid)\">Acanthopale (annelid)</a>.</div>\n\n<div class=\"wiki-table-scroll wiki-infobox-wrap\"><table class=\"infobox biota\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th colspan=\"2\"><i>Acanthopale</i>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\"><img class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"444\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Acanthopale.jpg/250px-Acanthopale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Acanthopale.jpg/500px-Acanthopale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"250\"></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th colspan=\"2\"><a data-title=\"Taxonomy (biology)\">Scientific classification</a> <span class=\"plainlinks taxobox-edit-taxonomy skin-invert\"><span><img alt=\"Edit this classification\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"15\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr.svg/40px-OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"15\"></span></span>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kingdom:\n</td>\n<td><a data-title=\"Plant\">Plantae</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"taxonrow\">\n<td><i>Clade</i>:\n</td>\n<td><a data-title=\"Vascular plant\">Tracheophytes</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"taxonrow\">\n<td><i>Clade</i>:\n</td>\n<td><a data-title=\"Flowering plant\">Angiosperms</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"taxonrow\">\n<td><i>Clade</i>:\n</td>\n<td><a data-title=\"Eudicots\">Eudicots</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"taxonrow\">\n<td><i>Clade</i>:\n</td>\n<td><a data-title=\"Asterids\">Asterids</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"taxonrow\">\n<td>Order:\n</td>\n<td><a data-title=\"Lamiales\">Lamiales</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"taxonrow\">\n<td>Family:\n</td>\n<td><a data-title=\"Acanthaceae\">Acanthaceae</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"taxonrow\">\n<td>Subfamily:\n</td>\n<td><a data-title=\"Acanthoideae\">Acanthoideae</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"taxonrow\">\n<td>Tribe:\n</td>\n<td><a data-title=\"Ruellieae\">Ruellieae</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"taxonrow\">\n<td>Genus:\n</td>\n<td><i>Acanthopale</i><br><small><a data-title=\"Charles Baron Clarke\">C.B.Clarke</a> (1899)</small>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th colspan=\"2\">Species\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p>12; see text\n</p>\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p><i><b>Acanthopale</b></i> is a <a data-title=\"Plant\">plant</a> genus of shrubs or subshrubs  in the <a data-title=\"Acanthaceae\">Acanthaceae</a> plant family. The <a data-title=\"Genus\">genus</a> name is based on the classic Greek words for thorn <i>\u00e1kantha</i> and stake <i>palum</i>. Some species in the genus are cultivated as <a data-title=\"Ornamental plant\">ornamental plants</a>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"wr-Species\">Species</h2></div>\n<p>12 species are accepted:\n</p>\n<ul><li><i>Acanthopale aethiogermanica</i> <span>Ensermu</span></li>\n<li><i>Acanthopale breviceps</i> <span>(Benoist) Callm. &amp; Phillipson</span></li>\n<li><i>Acanthopale cuneifolia</i> <span>(Benoist) Callm. &amp; Phillipson</span></li>\n<li><i>Acanthopale confertiflora</i> <span>(Lindau) C.B.Clarke</span></li>\n<li><i><a data-title=\"Acanthopale decempedalis\">Acanthopale decempedalis</a></i> <span>C.B.Clarke</span> (synonym <i>A. cameronica</i> <span>Bremek.</span>)</li>\n<li><i>Acanthopale humblotii</i> <span>(Benoist) Callm. &amp; Phillipson</span></li>\n<li><i>Acanthopale laxiflora</i> <span>(Lindau) C.B.Clarke</span> (syn. <i>Dischistocalyx laxiflorus</i> <span>Lindau</span>)</li>\n<li><i>Acanthopale macrocarpa</i> <small><a data-title=\"Kaj Borge Vollesen\">Vollesen</a></small></li>\n<li><i>Acanthopale madagascariensis</i> <span>(Baker) C.B.Clarke ex Bremek.</span></li>\n<li><i>Acanthopale perrieri</i> <span>(Benoist) Callm. &amp; Phillipson</span></li>\n<li><i><a data-title=\"Acanthopale pubescens\">Acanthopale pubescens</a></i> <span>(Lindau) C.B.Clarke</span></li>\n<li><i>Acanthopale ramiflora</i> <span>(Benoist) Callm. &amp; Phillipson</span></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"wr-Formerly_placed_here\">Formerly placed here</h3></div>\n<p><i>Dischistocalyx grandifolius</i> <span>C.B.Clarke</span> (as <i>Acanthopale buchholzii</i> <span>(Lindau) C.B.Clarke</span>)\n</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "links": ["Acanthopale (annelid)", "Taxonomy (biology)", "Plant", "Vascular plant", "Flowering plant", "Eudicots", "Asterids", "Lamiales", "Acanthaceae", "Acanthoideae", "Ruellieae", "Charles Baron Clarke", "Genus", "Ornamental plant", "Acanthopale decempedalis", "Kaj Borge Vollesen", "Acanthopale pubescens"]}